>
  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>
    Osamu Babasaki is an international business advisor specializing in brand strategy
    and overseas market development. With a career spanning diplomacy, government service,
    private enterprise, and brand business, he provides practical advisory services across
    European and Asian markets.
  </p>
  <p>
    His defining strength is <strong>going beyond strategy design to walk alongside clients through execution.</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>Career Foundation</h2>
  <p>
    Served at the Japan Ground Self-Defense Force Intelligence School, focusing on language
    education and Japan-U.S. joint training. Subsequently seconded to the Ministry of Foreign
    Affairs and posted as Consul to the Consulate General of Japan in West Berlin for four years.
    During this period, he built the practical foundation for international business through:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Cross-cultural communication</li>
    <li>International negotiation</li>
    <li>Relationship-building with public institutions</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Track Record in European Brand Business</h2>
  <p>
    After returning to the private sector, he led the Japan market entry of European luxury brands.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Herend (Hungary)</li>
    <li>Moser (Czech Republic)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    At their Japan exclusive distributors, he served as Trade Director and General Manager,
    driving brand introduction and market development through close coordination with embassies
    and commercial sections. His experience extends beyond importing — he has hands-on expertise
    in establishing brands within the Japanese market.
  </p>

  <h2>Business Development & IPO Track Record</h2>
  <p>
    At a trading company, he was involved in new business development with Toray, Teijin, and
    European partners. He later led an IPO project as Department Head, taking the company public
    on the Tokyo Stock Exchange Mothers market within three years. He subsequently served as
    Executive Managing Director, with a proven track record of not only crafting strategy but
    actually elevating enterprise value.
  </p>

  <h2>Fashion & International Brand Domain</h2>
  <p>At Yumi Katsura International, he served in international operations, including:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Participation in collections in Paris, Singapore, and Bangkok</li>
    <li>Management of the Paris boutique</li>
  </ul>
  <p>He brings real on-the-ground experience with global brands.</p>

  <h2>Founding Top Notch & Current Activities</h2>
  <p>
    Founded Top Notch Inc. and launched its brand business (Devon &amp; Drew Japan)
    alongside its international business advisory practice. Invited by Thailand's Ministry
    of Commerce, he delivered a brand strategy lecture in Bangkok to approximately 60
    young entrepreneurs.
  </p>
  <p>His current focus areas:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Thailand and the broader ASEAN market</li>
    <li>Japan market entry support</li>
  </ul>
  <p>He supports companies and brands in their international expansion.</p>

  <h2>What I Deliver</h2>
  <p>
    Babasaki's advisory differs from conventional consulting. He designs
    <strong>strategy that actually moves</strong>, not strategy on paper. Specifically:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Overseas market entry strategy design</li>
    <li>Brand positioning development</li>
    <li>Partner development (government and private)</li>
    <li>Small-batch execution support to minimize risk</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Approach</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Read the market through the field, not just data</li>
    <li>Prioritize an executable first step over a perfect plan</li>
    <li>Put relationship-building with partners first</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Strategy, execution, and relationship-building — designed as one.</p>

  <h2>Closing Message</h2>
  <blockquote>
    <p>We read the market, design the strategy, build partnerships, and execute the business.</p>
    <p>That is Top Notch's advisory.</p>
  </blockquote>
</PartnerLayout>
